<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Insein</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Insein is a township in the northern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Yangon</a>, Myanmar. In 1949, early in the Karen insurgency, Karen forces held Insein for more than three months, within a few miles of the capital, before government troops drove them out. It is known for Insein Prison, built under British rule, which held many political prisoners under military rule.</p></div>
